Privacy Policy for YouTube Focus

Last updated: November 2026

Zentube is a lightweight, privacy-first Chrome extension designed to help users reduce distractions and maintain focus while using YouTube.

1. Data Collection
Zentube does NOT collect, store, process, or transmit any personal data, browsing history, URLs, or user information to external servers. All operations and preference settings are performed and saved entirely locally on your device.

2. Use of Permissions
Zentube requests the absolute minimum permissions necessary to function. Here is exactly how each permission is used:

- storage: Used exclusively to save and load user interface preferences (e.g., toggle states for hiding Shorts, sidebars, or comments) locally on your device via chrome.storage.local. This data never leaves your browser.

- content_scripts: Used strictly to inject local CSS rules and a lightweight JavaScript listener into youtube.com pages. This allows the extension to hide specific UI elements based on your local preferences. We do NOT read, modify, track, or log the content of the pages, video playback, or your interactions with them.

3. Third-Party Sharing
We do not share any data with third parties, as no data is collected or transmitted outside of your local browser environment.
